---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Grey Knights Beginner's Guide — Warhammer 40k"
  description="New to Grey Knights? Learn how they play, how to paint their iconic silver armor, and exactly what to buy first for this elite psychic Space Marine faction."
>

  <!-- Hero -->
  <section class="px-6 pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#2a2a35]">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <a href="/factions/" class="text-sm text-[#4a4855] hover:text-[#8a8590] transition-colors mb-6 inline-block">
        ← All Factions
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
        <div class="text-6xl">🔱</div>
        <div>
          <p class="text-[#c9a84c] text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-2 font-display">Faction Guide</p>
          <h1 class="font-display text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">Grey Knights</h1>
          <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            The Imperium's most closely guarded secret. An entire Chapter of Space Marines who are
            also powerful psykers — created for one singular purpose: hunting and destroying Chaos
            daemons. Every single warrior. Every single one.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick stats -->
      <div class="mt-10 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Playstyle</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Elite Psychic</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Painting</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-yellow-400">Medium</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Rules</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm text-red-400">Hard</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4 text-center">
          <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] uppercase tracking-wide mb-1 font-display">Starter Cost</p>
          <p class="font-semibold text-sm">~$160</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Lore -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">Who are the Grey Knights?</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg">
        <p>
          They don't officially exist. The Imperium denies them. Witnesses are mind-wiped.
          The Grey Knights are based in a fortress-monastery on Titan, one of Saturn's moons,
          hidden behind a perpetual psychic veil. Even other Space Marine Chapters don't know
          their full truth. The Inquisition does — they work together, but carefully.
        </p>
        <p>
          What makes them unique: every single Grey Knight is a psyker. From the newest
          Battle-Brother to the Grand Master himself, every warrior in the Chapter wields
          psychic power. This isn't true of any other Space Marine Chapter in the Imperium.
          Their gene-seed draws from the same lineage as regular Marines, but has been
          further refined and augmented over ten thousand years of selective breeding and
          psychic conditioning.
        </p>
        <p>
          Their weapons — called Nemesis force weapons — are psychically charged blades and
          hammers that are devastatingly effective against daemonic entities. A Grey Knight
          Terminator carrying a force halberd is one of the most lethal anti-daemon weapons
          in the entire galaxy. They are also known for one other remarkable trait: no Grey
          Knight has ever fallen to Chaos. Not one, in ten thousand years. The mental
          conditioning runs that deep.
        </p>
        <p>
          Each Knight is said to know the true name of every greater daemon — and in the
          lore, knowing a daemon's true name gives you power over it. The Grey Knights
          are warriors, yes. But they are also scholars, mystics, and hunters of the
          most dangerous things that exist.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Playstyle -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-6">How they play on the table</h2>
      <div class="text-[#b8b4c0] leading-relaxed space-y-4 text-lg mb-10">
        <p>
          Grey Knights play small. Where a Space Marine army might field 30–50 models,
          a Grey Knights army typically runs <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">15–25 models total</strong>.
          These are among the most points-expensive infantry in the game — losing a single
          Terminator hurts. Every model counts in a way that few other armies can match.
        </p>
        <p>
          Their signature move is <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Deep Strike</strong> — teleporting
          units directly onto the battlefield mid-game. Combined with psychic powers from the
          Sanctic Sorcery discipline (offensive, defensive, and utility abilities), they can
          appear exactly where the threat is and immediately apply devastating pressure.
          Getting good positioning on your teleports is the core skill of the army.
        </p>
        <p>
          Combat is where they shine. Nemesis force weapons deal extra damage against daemons
          and pack psychic abilities that trigger on good dice rolls. The army is melee-forward
          with psychic support — not a shooty army. Resource management is critical: you have
          limited command points and psychic actions, and optimizing them each turn separates
          a good Grey Knights player from a great one.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is not the easiest army to learn. The low model count amplifies every mistake.
          But if you love precision, positioning puzzles, and the feeling of an elite strike
          force doing surgical damage — the reward is extraordinary.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-green-400">Grey Knights are for you if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✓ You love elite, low-model-count armies</li>
            <li>✓ You enjoy psychic/resource management gameplay</li>
            <li>✓ You want stunning silver armor that photographs beautifully</li>
            <li>✓ You love the idea of anti-daemon warrior-monks</li>
            <li>✓ You want a faction with incredible lore depth</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-5">
          <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-3 text-red-400">Maybe look elsewhere if...</h3>
          <ul class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm space-y-2">
            <li>✗ You're a complete beginner wanting a forgiving army</li>
            <li>✗ You want a horde with lots of cheap models on the table</li>
            <li>✗ You prefer shooting over melee</li>
            <li>✗ You don't want to think too hard about positioning</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Painting -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">How to paint Grey Knights</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-8 text-lg">
        Pure metallic silver — not gold like Custodes. The key look is clean, cold steel
        with glowing blue-purple psychic energy on the force weapons.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-4 mb-10">
        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">1</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Spray with Leadbelcher</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Citadel's metallic spray primer. Covers everything in one pass with a solid steel base coat. This is the foundation of the whole scheme.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">2</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Wash with Nuln Oil</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Flows into the panel lines and joints, creating instant shadow and depth on the silver armor. Let it dry fully — rushing this step muddies the final result.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">3</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Layer Ironbreaker on raised surfaces</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Restore the bright silver to the raised armor plates and edges while the Nuln Oil stays in the recesses. Use a flat brush and keep off the shadowed areas.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">4</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Edge highlight with Stormhost Silver</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">A thin bright line on the sharpest edges of every armor plate. This is what gives Grey Knights their crisp, heroic silhouette. Take your time — it's worth it.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">5</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Paint force weapons: psychic glow effect</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Base the blade with Kantor Blue → layer Caledor Sky over the upper two-thirds → edge with Lothern Blue → tip with White Scar. The result is a blade that looks like it's crackling with psychic energy.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex gap-4 bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-4">
          <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] font-bold font-display flex items-center justify-center flex-shrink-0 text-sm">6</div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-semibold text-sm mb-1">Red accents + gold trim + base</p>
            <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm">Mephiston Red for eye lenses and purity seals. Retributor Armour for any gold trim. Astrogranite Debris for the base, drybrush Administratum Grey, add a tuft.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Tip box -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-5">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold mb-2">The psychic glow shortcut</h3>
        <p class="text-[#b8b4c0] text-sm leading-relaxed">
          If you find the multi-layer blade technique intimidating, try
          <strong class="text-[#f0ede8]">Talassar Blue Contrast</strong> over a Wraithbone-primed blade.
          It creates a beautiful deep blue in one pass. Then just pick out the tip with White Scar.
          Much faster, still looks great on a gaming table.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- What to buy -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-2">What to buy first</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] mb-10 text-lg">Start with the Combat Patrol. Paint it before buying anything else.</p>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#c9a84c] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-4">
          <span class="bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113] text-xs font-semibold px-2 py-0.5 rounded font-display mr-2">Start Here</span>
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$160</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Combat Patrol: Grey Knights</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-3 leading-relaxed">
          Castellan Crowe (named hero), 10x Strike Squad (with alternate builds as Interceptors,
          Purifiers, or Purgation Squad), 5x Brotherhood Terminators (alternate: Paladin Squad),
          and 1x Venerable Dreadnought. 17 models — a complete, playable force.
        </p>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          The alternate build options are excellent value. The Strike Squad kit alone gives you
          four different unit types depending on how you assemble them — so this box builds
          the exact playstyle you want to focus on.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0FJ915PXJ?tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon for Combat Patrol →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6 mb-6">
        <div class="mb-3">
          <span class="text-xs text-[#4a4855]">~$60 · first expansion</span>
        </div>
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-2">Grey Knights Terminator Squad</h3>
        <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm mb-4 leading-relaxed">
          More Terminators are never wrong for Grey Knights. This box also builds Paladin Squad —
          the upgraded elite variant. Adding five more gives you the flexibility for different
          list configurations as you learn what playstyle you prefer.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=grey+knights+terminators+warhammer+40k&tag=grimdarkprime-20"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-5 py-2.5 rounded text-sm transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Search Amazon →
        </a>
      </div>

      <!-- Paints -->
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg p-6">
        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-xl mb-4">Paints you need</h3>
        <div class="space-y-3">
          {[
            { name: 'Leadbelcher Spray', use: 'Base coat — the silver foundation', required: true },
            { name: 'Nuln Oil', use: 'Shade wash — depth and shadow in joints', required: true },
            { name: 'Ironbreaker', use: 'Layer — restore bright silver on raised armor', required: true },
            { name: 'Stormhost Silver', use: 'Edge highlight — the final crisp shine', required: true },
            { name: 'Kantor Blue + Lothern Blue', use: 'Force weapon psychic glow', required: true },
            { name: 'Retributor Armour', use: 'Gold trim on purity seals and accents', required: false },
            { name: 'Mephiston Red', use: 'Eye lenses and purity seals', required: false },
          ].map(paint => (
            <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class={`text-xs px-2 py-0.5 rounded mt-0.5 flex-shrink-0 font-display ${paint.required ? 'bg-[#c9a84c] text-[#111113]' : 'border border-[#2a2a35] text-[#4a4855]'}`}>
                {paint.required ? 'Essential' : 'Optional'}
              </span>
              <div>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold">{paint.name}</span>
                <span class="text-[#8a8590] text-sm"> — {paint.use}</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6"><div class="border-t border-[#2a2a35]"></div></div>

  <!-- Cost breakdown -->
  <section class="px-6 py-16 bg-[#0d0d0f]">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] mb-8">Honest cost breakdown</h2>
      <div class="bg-[#1a1a1f] border border-[#2a2a35] rounded-lg overflow-hidden">
        {[
          { item: 'Combat Patrol: Grey Knights', cost: '~$160', note: '17 models — fully playable army' },
          { item: 'Essential paints (6)', cost: '~$40', note: 'Spray + shade + layers + force weapon colors' },
          { item: 'Basing supplies', cost: '~$12', note: 'Texture paint + tuft + grey' },
          { item: 'Clippers + hobby knife', cost: '~$20', note: 'One-time purchase' },
          { item: 'Superglue', cost: '~$5', note: 'Or plastic glue — both work' },
        ].map((row, i) => (
          <div class={`flex items-start justify-between px-5 py-4 gap-4 ${i % 2 === 0 ? '' : 'bg-[#111113]'}`}>
            <div>
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold">{row.item}</p>
              <p class="text-xs text-[#4a4855] mt-0.5">{row.note}</p>
            </div>
            <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#c9a84c] flex-shrink-0">{row.cost}</span>
          </div>
        ))}
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-5 py-4 bg-[#1f1d14] border-t border-[#c9a84c]">
          <p class="font-display font-semibold">All-in starter total</p>
          <span class="font-display font-bold text-[#c9a84c] text-lg">~$237</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-[#4a4855] text-sm mt-4 italic">
        Prices approximate. Grey Knights are an investment — but 17 elite models go a long
        way. You will not need to buy many more kits to have a competitive army.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CTA -->
  <section class="px-6 py-20 text-center">
    <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto">
      <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold mb-4">By the Emperor's Light.</h2>
      <p class="text-[#8a8590] text-lg mb-8">
        The Grey Knights are not for the faint of heart — on the table or in the hobby.
        But when that silver Terminator teleports in and carves through a Greater Daemon,
        there is nothing quite like it. The vigil never ends.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a
          href="/painting"
          class="inline-block bg-[#c9a84c] hover:bg-[#dfc070] text-[#111113] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display tracking-wide"
        >
          Painting Guide →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/quiz"
          class="inline-block border border-[#2a2a35] hover:border-[#c9a84c] text-[#b8b4c0] hover:text-[#c9a84c] font-semibold px-8 py-4 rounded text-lg transition-colors font-display"
        >
          Retake the Quiz
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
